WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.514
Hi! Take a deep breath... Can you feel the air going in? Today let's see where the air goes, and what carries oxygen around your body.

2
00:00:11.664 --> 00:00:16.746
Air is not just one gas. It is a mixture of several gases.

3
00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:24.018
Most of the air is nitrogen, about 78 percent. Next is oxygen, about 21 percent.

4
00:00:24.168 --> 00:00:29.802
There are also small amounts of carbon dioxide, water vapour and other gases.

5
00:00:29.952 --> 00:00:35.058
When we breathe, the gas our bodies need is oxygen.

6
00:00:35.208 --> 00:00:38.706
When we breathe in, air enters through the nose,

7
00:00:38.856 --> 00:00:41.514
passes down the windpipe,

8
00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:49.506
and goes into the two lungs. The lungs have many tiny air sacs, where oxygen from the air passes into the blood.

9
00:00:49.656 --> 00:00:55.986
At the same time, carbon dioxide passes from the blood into the lungs, and we breathe it out.

10
00:00:56.136 --> 00:01:08.442
So how does oxygen reach the whole body? Through the circulatory system. The heart is like a pump. It pushes blood through blood vessels to every part of the body.

11
00:01:08.592 --> 00:01:16.050
Let's compare the air we breathe in and out. Exhaled air has less oxygen, because the body has used some.

12
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:22.362
Exhaled air has more carbon dioxide, because the body produces carbon dioxide.

13
00:01:22.512 --> 00:01:30.450
Exhaled air also has more water vapour. That's why a cold mirror mists up when you breathe on it.

14
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.730
Blood carries oxygen and digested food to the cells all over the body.

15
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.938
Blood also takes away carbon dioxide and wastes made by the cells.

16
00:01:41.088 --> 00:01:50.226
When you run, your body needs more oxygen. So you breathe faster, your heart beats faster, and your pulse rate goes up.

17
00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:58.458
Watch out! Some pupils say we breathe in only oxygen and breathe out only carbon dioxide. That's wrong!

18
00:01:58.608 --> 00:02:07.314
We breathe in air and breathe out air, both mixtures of gases. Exhaled air just has less oxygen and more carbon dioxide.

19
00:02:07.464 --> 00:02:13.722
Exhaled air still contains oxygen, and lots of nitrogen too.

20
00:02:13.872 --> 00:02:22.218
Your turn! Which gas makes up most of the air? Pause and think.

21
00:02:22.368 --> 00:02:29.418
It's nitrogen, about 78 percent, not oxygen. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:29.568 --> 00:02:38.778
Another one! Where in the body does oxygen pass into the blood? Pause and think.

23
00:02:38.928 --> 00:02:44.490
In the tiny air sacs in the lungs. Did you get it right?

24
00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:53.346
Last one! Why does your heart beat faster after you run? Pause and think.

25
00:02:53.496 --> 00:03:02.346
Because the body needs more oxygen and food, so the heart pumps blood around the body faster. Did you get it right?

26
00:03:02.496 --> 00:03:16.794
Remember: air goes from the nose down the windpipe into the lungs, where oxygen enters the blood. The heart pumps blood through blood vessels to the whole body, delivering oxygen and food and taking away carbon dioxide and wastes.

27
00:03:16.944 --> 00:03:21.090
Jump around, then feel your pulse!

